%----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% readme_HMR_System_pars_bif_vt.txt
%----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% In this directory we use the NGRC DDE system in order to reproduce the
% bifurcation tree for the HMR neuron system;
% The NGRC DDE system is learned from the x(t) signal of HMR neuron system;
% During learning we impose the requirement for the Transversal Lyapunov 
% Exponent (TLE) to be some negative value;
% The learning is performed at several system parameters; subsequently,
% we scan the system parameter, and compute the bifurcations with NGRC DDE;
%----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Below we list the main files in this directory;
%----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% HMR_X_ngrc_par_aut_v6.m -> in this file we integrate the closed NGRC DDE
% system after learning; it is useful for searching optimal NGRC DDE system's
% parameters; the file uses the auxiliary function [HMR_signal.m]; it
% is necessary to produce the exact time series which will be used for
% learning of the NGRC DDE system;
%----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% HMR_X_ngrc_bif_diagram_v6.m -> this file computes the whole bifurcation
% diagram from NGRC DDE system after learning at several parameters values;
% this file uses the auxiliary function [HMR_signal_v2.m] to produce the 
% exact time series of HMR system;  
%----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% plot_bif_tot_v.m -> this program plots the bifurcation diagrams, computed from the
% both sources: from exact HMR neurons system, and from the NGRC DDE system;
% this function is used by program
% [HMR_X_ngrc_bif_diagram_v6.m];
%----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% HMR_signal_v2.m -> this auxiliary function computes the dynamics of 
% original HMR system; this function makes a "warming up" before computing the
% necessary time series; the "warming up" means that the system is run for a long
% time and it's dynamics is not recorded; this procedure is useful as one
% changes the system parameter; this function is used by program
% [HMR_X_ngrc_bif_diagram_v6.m];
%----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% These files are auxiliary functions for the NGRC DDE system:
%----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% generate_all_exp_matreces.m
% generateCheb_feat_vect.m
% generateChebyshevs.m
% generateChebyshevsDiffLyap.m
% genExponents.m
%----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% matr.mat -> contains power matrices necessary for composing Tschebyshev
% polynomials;
%----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% result_ngrc_v6t.mat -> data file, contains the results of computions of
% bifurcation diagram with NGRC DDE system; this file is computed by
% program [HMR_X_ngrc_bif_diagram_v6.m];
%----------------------------------------------------------------------------
